~$*

# Supporting Documents/ holds real customer quotations the desk supplied as
# reference. Only a comment in shared/company.ts points at them; nothing loads
# them, so they are handed over separately rather than cloned seven times.
#
# Resources/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the Tally sundry-debtors export,
# and importCustomers.test.ts reads it directly — 33 tests assert against the
# real file, because every quirk they guard (Tally's \x04 before "Not
# Applicable", addresses flattened into one cell, a GSTIN with a trailing
# carriage return) came out of that spreadsheet and a hand-built fixture would
# not carry them. Excluding it would make those tests vanish silently in CI.
Supporting Documents/
